e9cc17c
Port FileIndex checkpoint-loss and journal isolation tests to per-drive watches

Ports FileIndexCacheOnlyUnresumableWatchTests, FileIndexMidSessionCheckpointLossTests
and ConsumerJournalIsolationTests onto the per-drive contract. FileIndexCheckpointLossDetectionTests
was already ported by B1 and is unchanged.

Renamed (old name states something no longer true):
- StartWatchingAsync_LeavesTheUnresumableDriveOutAndWatchesTheHealthyOne ->
  StartWatchingAsync_RefusesTheUnresumableDriveAndWatchesTheHealthyOne
- RescanAsync_OnTheUnresumableDriveWhileWatching_ClearsTheRefusalAndArmsItOntoTheRunningWatch ->
  RescanAsync_OnTheUnresumableDrive_ClearsTheRefusalAndLeavesTheDriveReadyToStart
- RescanAsync_OnTheUnresumableDriveWhileWatching_WhenTheScanFailsWithoutThrowing_LeavesTheRefusalIntact ->
  RescanAsync_OnTheUnresumableDrive_WhenTheScanFailsWithoutThrowing_LeavesTheRefusalIntact
- StartWatchingAsync_WhenEveryMftDriveIsUnresumable_StartsNoSessionButReportsEachDrive ->
  StartWatchingAsync_WhenTheOnlyMftDriveIsUnresumable_RefusesItAndReportsIt
- SourceEndingWithoutAStop_ClassifiesEveryWatchedDrive ->
  WatchEndingWithoutAStop_ClassifiesEachDriveAgainstItsOwnJournal

Dropped:
- RescanAsync_StartedBeforeAnyWatchSession_StillArmsTheRecoveredDriveOntoASessionThatStartedMidScan:
  pins a session captured at suspend time and a session started mid-scan; there is no session.
- WatchFaultOnADriveWithNoBlock_QueriesNoJournal: pins a fault announced for a drive letter with
  no block, which only a shared stream could carry; a per-drive watch starts only over an MFT block.

Added:
- WatchFaultOnT_LiveWatchLossRecordedBeforeWatchFaultedRaised: the handler reads the loss.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>

---
6b6aa35
Port FileIndex watch, pump, fault and catch-up tests to per-drive watches

Ports FileIndexWatchTests, FileIndexWatchPumpTests, FileIndexWatchFaultTests,
FileIndexWatchCatchUpTests and FileIndexWatchCatchUpLinkedWaitTests onto
FakeIndexWatchSource, ScriptedDriveWatch and WatchHarness. No test support
member was added or changed.

Renamed (old name states something no longer true):
- FileIndexWatchTests.StartWatchingAsync_OnAnEnumerationOnlyIndex_CompletesWithoutCallingSource
  -> StartWatchingAsync_OnAnEnumerationDrive_ThrowsWithoutCallingSource
- Pump.StartWatchingAsync_PassesEveryDriveCursorToOneSourceInvocation
  -> StartWatchingAsync_EachDriveStartsFromItsOwnHeaderCursor
- Pump.WatchFaulted_AnnouncesASourceFaultWithNoDriveLetter
  -> WatchFaulted_AnnouncesAChannelFaultNamingTheDrive
- Pump.WatchFaulted_ReportsAnIndependentSourceOperationCanceledException
  -> StartWatchingAsync_ReportsAnIndependentSourceOperationCanceledExceptionThroughTheStart
- Pump.SourceCompletingWithoutAStop_FaultsEveryWatchedDriveAndReleasesTheSession
  -> HandleEndingWithoutAStop_FaultsTheDriveAndAFreshStartRecovers
- Pump.StartWatchingAsync_AfterStop_RecordsFaultsForTheNewSession
  -> StartWatchingAsync_AfterStop_RecordsFaultsForTheNewWatch
- Fault.ApplyFailure kept; DriveWatchFailure_IsReportedAsASourceFaultCarryingTheDriveLetter
  -> DriveFailure_IsReportedAsADriveFaultCarryingTheDriveLetter
- Fault.WholeStreamFault_EndsThePumpAndNamesNoDrive
  -> ChannelLoss_EndsOnlyThatDrivesPump_AndNamesTheDrive
- Fault.EveryDriveFaulted_EndsThePumpAndLeavesTheFirstFaultForStop
  -> EveryDriveFaulted_LeavesEachDrivesFaultForItsOwnStop
- Fault.CallerTokenCancellation_EndsTheWatchWithNoFault
  -> CallerTokenCancellation_DuringStart_EndsTheStartWithNoFault (plus new
     CallerTokenCancellation_AfterStart_LeavesTheWatchRunning: the start token
     bounds only the start)
- Fault.StopWatchingAsync_WithACancelledToken_AbandonsTheWaitAndLeavesTheSessionReclaimable
  -> ..._AbandonsTheWaitAndLeavesTheDriveRestartable
- Fault.StartAfterStop_LeavesNoOrphanedSessionAndClearsEveryWatchFailure
  -> StartAfterStop_LeavesNoOrphanedHandleAndClearsTheWatchFailure
- CatchUp.StartWatchingAsync_BeginsCatchingUpEveryWatchedDrive
  -> StartWatchingAsync_BeginsCatchingUpTheDrive
- CatchUp.DriveWatchFailure_FaultsTheDrivesCatchUp
  -> DriveFailure_FaultsTheDrivesCatchUp
- CatchUp.SourceCompletingWithoutAStop_FaultsEveryDrivesCatchUp
  -> HandleEndingWithoutAStop_FaultsTheDrivesCatchUp
- CatchUp.WaitForCatchUpAsync_SourceException_FaultsPendingWait
  -> WaitForCatchUpAsync_ChannelLoss_FaultsPendingWait

Dropped:
- Pump.StartWatchingAsync_ThrowsWhenADriveSupportsWatchAndNoSourceIsConfigured:
  no source is configured only in FileIndexWatchTests, which keeps
  StartWatchingAsync_OnAMixedIndexWithoutASource_ThrowsInvalidOperation.
- Pump.StartWatchingAsync_WhenAlreadyWatching_ThrowsInvalidOperation: the
  contract is inverted (a drive already watching is left alone), covered by
  FileIndexPerDriveWatchTests.StartWatching_AlreadyWatching_DoesNotRestart.
- Pump.StopWatchingAsync_BeforeAWatchStarts_HasNoEffect: the contract is
  inverted (stopping a drive that is not watching throws), covered by
  FileIndexPerDriveWatchTests.Stop_DriveNeverStarted_ThrowsInvalidOperation.
- Fault.ApplyFailure_OnADriveWithNoBlock_IsAnnouncedWithoutADriveStatusMessage:
  a batch names no drive and a handle belongs to one drive; routing to a
  drive with no block cannot happen.
- Fault.ApplyFailure_OnADriveWithNoBlock_IsAnnouncedOnceHoweverOftenItRepeats:
  same, and the pump's dropped-letter set is gone.
- Fault.DriveWatchFailure_RepeatedForTheSameDrive_IsAnnouncedOnlyOnce: a
  handle's read fails once and its pump has ended; there is no repeat item.
- CatchUp.DriveCaughtUpItem_ForAFaultedDriveIsIgnored: a faulted drive's pump
  has ended and its handle takes no further items.
- CatchUp.WaitForCatchUpAsync_SessionCancellation_CancelsPendingWait: the
  start token bounds only the start; there is no session token.
- CatchUp.WaitForCatchUpAsync_AllDrives_* (10 methods: WaitsForTheSlowestDrive,
  WithASingleWatchedDrive_CompletesWithItsCatchUp,
  WhenEveryDriveAlreadyCaughtUp_IsCompleteAtIssue, ThrowsWhenNoWatchIsRunning,
  FaultsImmediatelyWhenFirstDriveFaultsWhileSecondIsCatchingUp,
  DriveFaultsAfterCatchUpWhileOtherDriveIsCatchingUp,
  DriveReArmedAfterCatchUpWhileOtherDriveIsCatchingUp_CancelsAggregateWait,
  DriveFaultsAfterCatchUpThenOtherDriveCatchesUp_FaultsAggregateWait,
  DriveFaultsWhileCatchingUpThenOtherDriveCatchesUp_FaultsAggregateWait,
  DriveReArmedWhileCatchingUpThenOtherDriveCatchesUp_CancelsAggregateWait):
  the no-list wait arrives in task B7, which covers the batched wait.
  The all-drives half of WaitForCatchUpAsync_DriveFaultsAfterCatchUp_ReturnsFaultedTask
  is dropped with them.
- LinkedWait.WaitForCatchUpAsync_AllDrivesWithoutACallerToken_WhenDisposed_CancelsTheCoordinator:
  the catch-up coordinator no longer exists.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>

