- Fault.ApplyFailure_OnADriveWithNoBlock_IsAnnouncedWithoutADriveStatusMessage:
  a batch names no drive and a handle belongs to one drive; routing to a
  drive with no block cannot happen.
- Fault.ApplyFailure_OnADriveWithNoBlock_IsAnnouncedOnceHoweverOftenItRepeats:
  same, and the pump's dropped-letter set is gone.
- Fault.DriveWatchFailure_RepeatedForTheSameDrive_IsAnnouncedOnlyOnce: a
  handle's read fails once and its pump has ended; there is no repeat item.
- CatchUp.DriveCaughtUpItem_ForAFaultedDriveIsIgnored: a faulted drive's pump
