---
25c45fa
Host heartbeats idle pipes and reports a wedged operation as Stalled

Every host pipe (the control pipe and each drive pipe) gets a HostPipeWriter:
its write lock, a wrote-since-last-visit flag, and the ChannelOperationState its
loop and its source publish (it is the IBrokerOperationReporter sources receive).
A frame write or a publication restarts the pipe's progress clock.

BrokerHeartbeatSender runs on one dedicated background thread per session,
woken every HeartbeatInterval by a TimeProvider timer. Per visit it skips a pipe
that wrote since the last visit or has a write in flight (non-blocking lock
attempt), heartbeats the idle control pipe and WaitingOnVolume or Queued drive
pipes, and for a Processing step past ProcessingLimit writes Stalled naming the
step, then cancels that channel. The sender only starts writes; it never waits
for one.

Scans publish WaitingOnVolume around the cursor's volume open, Processing per
record batch and per flushed block range (RealBlockSectionWriter passes a range
reporter to BlockWriter.Complete), and read catch-up in bounded calls of
CatchUpBufferReadsPerCall journal buffers, republishing per call that advanced
the cursor; a failed call is not retried and the journal check chooses
CatchUpLost or Error. The watch loop publishes WaitingOnVolume before each read
and Processing per batch. The progress pump throttles on the host's clock.

UsnJournalCatchUpSource gains maximumBufferReads; IBlockSectionWriter.Write takes
BlockWriteReporting (progress plus operation reporter). BrokerOperationState is
replaced by ChannelOperationState and HostPipeWriter. The public
JournalBrokerHost.CatchUp is deleted; its test
CatchUp_DelegatesToReadJournal_ReturnsAdvancedCursor is dropped because the
single-call delegation it pinned no longer exists.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>

