+### Summary
+
+Affected file means a base test file deleted at least once in 3597586..HEAD. Counts are method occurrences; same-name matching is repository-wide at HEAD.
+
+| tranche | base methods in affected files | ported same name | renamed | dropped with reason | not accounted for |
+| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
+| B | 420 | 106 | 34 | 85 | 195 |
+| I | 150 | 69 | 23 | 14 | 44 |
+
+The complete inventory contained 1,717 base methods (1,709 unique names) and 1,701 HEAD methods (1,693 unique names). Global reconciliation, including files never deleted in the range, is:
+
+| tranche | all base methods | present same name | renamed | dropped with reason | not accounted for |
+| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
+| B | 462 | 146 | 34 | 87 | 195 |
+| I | 1255 | 1165 | 26 | 14 | 50 |
+
+Six Tranche I not-accounted names are outside deleted files: two FileIndexRescanCleanup methods, three ABI-version-1 methods, and EndWatch_IdleNativeRead_Acknowledges. They remain below because the requested comparison covered every absent base name.
+
+One renamed absent method had DataRows: FaultRecordedDuringFailedProduction_IsKeptAndOldCursorIsNotRearmed had ("running"), ("ended"), and ("stream-ended"). Its commit mapping was validated against the replacement at HEAD.
+
